From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikael Hug <mikaelhug@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:46:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/prep/hw-audio-4' into
 prep/hw-test5

sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c merged without a textual conflict, but the
result was wrong. hw-audio-4 40423999045a adds the else branch that turns
off the sense transmit, using "return ret" on its errors. review/audio
e87870fbd701 turned the probe error paths into "goto err_disable_reg".
Two of the three error returns in the sense block were left as
"return ret", which would keep the amplifier regulator enabled and SDZ
high after a failed probe. All three now use goto err_disable_reg.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UqitcmCNS6G33aQUShi39x
---
 sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
index 7fbece7..e876702 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
@@ -816,7 +816,16 @@ static int tas2764_codec_probe(struct snd_soc_component *component)
 	if (tas2764->i_sense_slot != -1 && tas2764->v_sense_slot != -1) {
 		ret = tas2764_set_ivsense_transmit(tas2764, tas2764->i_sense_slot,
 						   tas2764->v_sense_slot);
+		if (ret < 0)
+			goto err_disable_reg;
+	} else {
+		ret = snd_soc_component_update_bits(component, TAS2764_TDM_CFG5,
+						    TAS2764_TDM_CFG5_VSNS_ENABLE, 0);
+		if (ret < 0)
+			goto err_disable_reg;
 
+		ret = snd_soc_component_update_bits(component, TAS2764_TDM_CFG6,
+						    TAS2764_TDM_CFG6_ISNS_ENABLE, 0);
 		if (ret < 0)
 			goto err_disable_reg;
 	}
